Subject: Adapt original queued dispatch and payload lifetimes

Upstream-base: 2c5c51e483b652d178ef06a44b83b07a0f97d2a6

Retain original callback order and one-batch/full-drain modes with native
counter widths, transactional callback insertion, exception/cancellation cleanup,
and destruction before slot-pool release. Native event tokens cancel pending
payloads before event destruction and reject a destroyed dispatcher. Rejected
Queue calls retain caller payload ownership. Original callbacks remain game-owned.
Runtime helpers implement checked bounds and exactly-once disposal in src/.
Full game task/frame wiring and pre-main event construction remain unselected.

